---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Project Data Science Guild" windowTitle="web project" showCloseBtn={true}>
  <div class="projectWindow">
    <div class="lg-5" data-inView="slideIn">
      <div class="textbox jc">
        <h2>Project Data Science Guild</h2>
        <p>For this project, I had the opportunity to work with SharePoint and use its list feature as a pseudo back-end to save data.</p>
        <p>SharePoint is a powerful platform that allows businesses to collaborate and manage their data efficiently, and I was excited to explore its capabilities in web development.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lg-8 lg-offset-3" data-inView="slideInRight">
      <div class="bitFilter">
        <video playsinline loop autoplay muted data-lazyVideo>
          <source src="/media/projects/dsg-About-1920.mp4" type='video/mp4' />
        </video>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="lg-10" data-inView="slideInUp">
      <div class="bitFilter">
        <img  class="lazy" src="/media/small/dsg_mobile.png" data-hiResImg="/media/projects/dsg_mobile.webp" alt="">
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="lg-10 lg-offset-2" data-inView="slideInUp">
      <div class="bitFilter">
        <video playsinline loop autoplay muted data-lazyVideo>
          <source src="/media/projects/tablet-skills.mp4" type='video/mp4' />
        </video>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lg-7" data-inView="slideInRight">
      <div class="textbox jc">
        <p>Using SharePoint lists as a back-end allowed me to create a seamless user experience, where data can be saved and retrieved easily without the need for complex databases. It also provided a centralized location for data management, ensuring that information is consistent and up-to-date across the website.</p>
        <p>I believe that using the right tools and technologies is essential to creating successful websites, and SharePoint is one such tool that has proven its worth in data management and collaboration. I am always eager to learn and explore new technologies to create better and more efficient websites for my clients.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
